i think the real key to what we did on  superman that made it work was  we really all did check our egos at the  door  superman was the only person that  mattered it was always about the stories  it was always about  where are we going with this stuff  whenever we had a problem  it would be  shouted out let's just kill him  and this was the time where i said okay  wise guys if we kill him then what  happens i says i think we better not  screw up  because this is one of those things we  can do once  we just all agreed and knew that we  didn't want kryptonite to kill him we  didn't want lex luthor to kill him it  had to be something new it had to be  something different and we all voted on  doomsday  at the meeting and we all picked dan's  version from a personality standpoint  the doomsday is so much the opposite  from what superman is you take superman  away  to make people realize that they  actually cared about him and missed him  we really did get the comic stores  interested and we got a lot of new  readers out of it as well you meet  people who at comic book conventions and  they say  oh this was my first comic whole  families were coming out uncles and  aunts  the announcement of this anniversary  edition with all new material has really  gotten a lot of attention even seeing  all the work come across on the 30th  anniversary special  is is a lot of fun to see everybody  working together again for my story it  takes place  a couple of years ago so  young john kent is now about nine or ten  years old and one day someone comes into  school and he's wearing a black armband  with the shield on and he said i'm here  to talk about  one of the most famous days in the  history of metropolis which is the day  that superman died  and young john kept sits there and he  says what that sets us off on a story  that can take us through  kind of a retrospective of what happened  in metropolis during those times and  also  a new villain called doom breaker that  comes into the superman universe now  what was really fun for me in creating a  new superman story was really as  creating a steel story a john henry  irons before he puts on the armor it's  the  15-20 minutes before superman's death  and what he's doing i have to admit i've  always loved  jack kirby's guardian character and  basically have  the guardian's point of view of all  these crazy things were going on  during the  superman and doomsday's chase across  country to metropolis my first thought  on it was really to do something with  mom and pop kent i thought of the  you know just the horrible aspect of  being parents and watching you know  nobody else knows that's your son all  three of the stories are really nice and  i think really will  touch readers it's just great to see  this these collections come out  periodically to remind people  that this was a big deal  [Music]  you
 

